---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import GenerationPage from "../components/GenerationPage.jsx";

---

<BaseLayout
	title="Algorithmic Art Gallery | Generative art by Jonathan R Reed"
	description="Generate algorithmic artworks with curated controls, live previews, saved gallery studies, deterministic seeds, and high-resolution exports by Jonathan R Reed."
>
	<section class="art-index-intro" aria-labelledby="art-index-title">
		<p class="mono-text">Generative art studio</p>
		<h1 id="art-index-title">Algorithmic Art Gallery</h1>
		<p class="mono-text">
			By Jonathan R Reed. Updated <time datetime="2026-04-21">April 21, 2026</time>.
		</p>
		<p>
			Build deterministic artwork from space-filling curves, growth modes,
			color ordering, symmetry rules, and seed controls. Every saved output
			can be regenerated from the same settings, then exported for sharing or
			printing.
		</p>
		<p>
			The studio is designed for deliberate exploration rather than random
			effects. Use the controls to compare Hilbert and Morton traversal,
			change how color moves through the image, then save the strongest
			variations into the gallery for later review.
		</p>
		<p>
			Start with a seed, choose a growth model, then watch the system build a
			composition from repeatable rules. The same settings always recreate
			the same result, which makes it easier to study small changes in curve
			order, symmetry, color distance, and export size.
		</p>
		<p>
			Use the first run as a baseline, then adjust one variable at a time to
			see how the image responds. This makes the gallery useful for both
			playful exploration and a more deliberate study of visual systems.
		</p>
		<p>
			Finished pieces can be saved for comparison, revisited from the gallery,
			and exported at larger sizes when a pattern is strong enough to keep.
		</p>
		<p>
			The controls are intentionally exposed so the artwork stays explainable.
			A seed defines the starting point, a traversal curve determines how the
			canvas is visited, and the color rules decide how structure becomes
			visible. That makes each image easier to discuss, repeat, and refine.
		</p>
		<p>
			For best results, compare a few related outputs instead of chasing a
			single perfect image. Small parameter changes often reveal the visual
			logic behind a piece more clearly than a completely new random seed.
		</p>
		<div class="art-index-links">
			<a href="/gallery/">Browse gallery</a>
			<a href="/about/">How it works</a>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Minimalist Brutal Loader -->
	<div class="art-loader" id="art-loader">
		<div class="loader-container">
			<div class="brutal-spinner"></div>
			<div class="loader-text mono-text">[INITIALIZING SYSTEM]</div>
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="generator-container">
		<GenerationPage client:only="react" />
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<script is:inline>
	// Hide loader when React component loads
	const checkReactLoaded = () => {
		const loader = document.getElementById("art-loader");
		const generator = document.querySelector(".generator-container");
		if (generator && generator.children.length > 0) {
			if (loader) {
				loader.classList.add("fade-out");
				setTimeout(() => {
					loader.style.display = "none";
				}, 500);
			}
		} else {
			requestAnimationFrame(checkReactLoaded);
		}
	};
	// Start checking after a brief delay
	setTimeout(checkReactLoaded, 100);
</script>

<style>
	/* ========================================
	   BRUTAL MINIMAL LOADER
	   ======================================== */
	.art-loader {
		position: fixed;
		inset: 0;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		z-index: 50;
		background: var(--color-paper);
		opacity: 1;
		transition: opacity 0.3s ease;
	}

	.art-loader.fade-out {
		opacity: 0;
		pointer-events: none;
	}

	.loader-container {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 1.5rem;
		background: var(--color-paper-alt);
		padding: 2rem 4rem;
		border: var(--border-ink);
		box-shadow: 12px 12px 0 0 var(--color-ink);
	}

	.brutal-spinner {
		width: 40px;
		height: 40px;
		border: 4px solid var(--color-ink);
		border-right-color: transparent;
		animation: spin 0.8s linear infinite;
	}

	.loader-text {
		color: var(--color-ink);
		font-weight: 600;
		animation: blink 1s step-end infinite;
	}

	@keyframes spin {
		from {
			transform: rotate(0deg);
		}
		to {
			transform: rotate(360deg);
		}
	}

	@keyframes blink {
		0%,
		100% {
			opacity: 1;
		}
		50% {
			opacity: 0;
		}
	}

	.generator-container {
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 1240px;
		padding: 0 1rem;
		box-sizing: border-box;
	}

	.art-index-intro {
		width: min(1120px, calc(100% - 2rem));
		margin: 0 auto 1.5rem;
		padding: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
		border: var(--border-ink);
		background: var(--color-paper-alt);
		box-shadow: 8px 8px 0 0 var(--color-ink);
	}

	.art-index-intro h1 {
		margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;
		color: var(--color-ink);
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 8vw, 5.5rem);
		line-height: 0.95;
	}

	.art-index-intro p {
		max-width: 70ch;
		color: var(--color-muted);
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	.art-index-links {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
	}

	.art-index-links a {
		border: var(--border-ink);
		background: var(--color-paper);
		color: var(--color-ink);
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
		text-decoration: none;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.art-index-links a:hover {
		background: var(--color-ink);
		color: var(--color-paper);
	}

	@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
		.brutal-spinner {
			animation: none;
			border-right-color: var(--color-ink);
		}
		.loader-text {
			animation: none;
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 768px) {
		.generator-container {
			padding: 0 0.75rem;
		}
	}
</style>
